{"title":"Rusty Axe","slug":"Rusty_Axe","hero":null,"pageid":284,"revid":20541,"timestamp":"2025-11-25T23:07:38Z","lastEditor":"Anty2013","categories":["Tools","Axes"],"infobox":{"type":"Axe","fields":[{"label":"Island","value":"Finlay"},{"label":"Shop","value":"The Oak Depot"},{"label":"Swing Power","value":"0.24"},{"label":"Swing Distance","value":"12 studs"},{"label":"Swing Time","value":"0.85"},{"label":"Price","value":"$390"},{"label":"Version Added","value":"v1.0.0"},{"label":"Date Added","value":"14/0/2023"}]},"sections":[{"id":"description","text":"Description"},{"id":"appearance","text":"Appearance"},{"id":"trivia","text":"Trivia"}],"body":"<blockquote><p><i><big>\"It's definitely better than a wooden one, that's for sure\"</big></i></p></blockquote>\n\n<h2 id=\"description\">Description</h2>\n<p>Rusty Axe is an axe that players start with when creating a fresh save. It's the second worst axe in the game, being also sold in basement of <a href=\"__BASE__/wiki/The_Oak_Depot/\">The Oak Depot</a> for $390.\n</p>\n<h2 id=\"appearance\">Appearance</h2>\n<p>Rusty axe is acting as an improvised grip, while being made out of typical yellow wood, using the default legacy wood material.\n</p>\n<h2 id=\"trivia\">Trivia</h2>\n<ul><li>The Rusty Axe replaced the <a href=\"__BASE__/wiki/Wooden_Axe/\">Wooden Axe</a> as the best axe.</li>\n<li>A Rusty Axe can be found at <a href=\"__BASE__/wiki/Mike's_Mines/\">Mike's Mines</a> but cannot be picked up and bought.</li>\n<li>The Rusty Axe can also be found on stumps.</li></ul>\n\n<figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"> \t<span role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Media not yet archived: A Rusty Axe found on a stump, not placed there as it has no owner.\">A Rusty Axe found on a stump, not placed there as it has no owner.</span> \t \t<figcaption> \t\t \t\t\t<span data-unresolved=\"1\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></span> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p>A Rusty Axe found on a stump, not placed there as it has no owner.</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>"}
